      "message": "This is where I made a conscious choice to deviate from the c++23 spec and take the size from the first argument.  Then, we avoid any sort of bounds-checking safe-iterator on a step-by-step basis, rather check once at construction time that the other ranges are big enough.\n\nThis requires sized-rages, and makes but a single check at advance time rather than checking N iterators to see if any has hit an end.\n\nCan you take a look at the resulting assy for a simple loop and check if we regress when we go to base::zip?",
